.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.LOCAL.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.local.mk
.Nd per-level hook files
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Reads a level's hook files, for local settings that do not belong in the shared
files.
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Pp
Every level may have an
.Pa mk/
directory, and each is searched for, in this order:
.Bl -tag -width "pre.TARGET_TARGET_ARCH.mk" -offset indent -compact
.It Pa pre.mk , local.mk
always
.It Pa pre. Ns Va TOOLCHAIN Ns Pa .mk
for one toolchain
.It Pa pre. Ns Va TARGET Ns Pa .mk
for one system
.It Pa pre. Ns Va TARGET Ns Pa _ Ns Va TARGET_ARCH Ns Pa .mk
for one system and architecture
.El
.Pp
.Pa local Ns Pa .*
has the same variants.
.Pa pre
files are read after the target is known and before the role file sets its
defaults;
.Pa local
files at the end.
.Pp
All levels that have a file are read, outermost first, so an inner one can
override:
.Bl -column "Framework" "each parent, workspace, framework, module" -offset indent
.It Sy From Ta Sy Reads Pa mk/ Sy in
.It Workspace Ta each parent, then its own
.It Framework Ta each parent, workspace, its own
.It Module Ta each parent, workspace, framework, its own
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
A Homebrew path on one architecture, in
.Pa mk/pre.macos_arm64.mk :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
IMPORT_PREFIX=/opt/homebrew
.Ed
.Pp
One more flag for one toolchain, in
.Pa mk/local.gcc.mk :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
CFLAGS+=-fno-strict-aliasing
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mk.common.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.framework.mk 5 ,
.Xr mk.workspace.mk 5 ,
.Xr bmake-it 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
.Sh CAVEATS
There is no name combining toolchain and architecture.
